<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hou Jing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">503–552</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hou Jing was a general of Eastern Wei who defected to the southern Liang dynasty after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-huan">Gao Huan</a> in 547. In 548 he rebelled, besieged the Liang capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a> and took it in 549, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-liang">Emperor Wu of Liang</a> died in his hands. He proclaimed himself emperor of Han in 551 but was defeated by Liang forces under Wang Sengbian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-chen">Chen Baxian</a> and killed in 552. His rebellion devastated southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hou-jing.jpg" alt="Hou Jing" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hou_Jing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
